<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Avar campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/791">791</a>–803</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Avar campaigns</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> campaign was a series of wars waged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> and his commanders against the Avar Khaganate in the Pannonian basin between 791 and 803. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> captured the Avars' fortified 'Ring' and seized a great treasure. The campaigns ended Avar power and extended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>'s influence to the south-east.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Avar campaigns</b> of the 790s destroyed the power of the Avar khaganate in Pannonia and brought back so much treasure, reportedly fifteen wagons, each drawn by four oxen, that it transformed Carolingian finances.</blockquote><a href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
